  "best_idea": "Step timing from distance travelled times a per-creature tempo (not from frame time), with one stored pose blended toward the target each frame, so a creature's legs stay in step with its speed and frame rate does not change the gait.",
  "decision": "adapt",
  "decision_why": "Frankendom's creatures need the distance phase and the one stored pose, but the donor's accumulator is unsigned (a back-step looks like a stride) and its per-frame blend snaps on long frames; we keep the shape, sign the phase, use exponential blending and move tempo and mount offsets into catalogue data.",
  "decision_status": "proposed",
  "acceptance": "A creature with tempo 0.9 walking at 6 units per second takes the same steps per metre on a 30 fps and a 144 fps client; on stopping the pose reaches 90 percent of the idle target in about 0.15 s with no snap on a 100 ms hitch; a rider keeps the same offset in the mount bone frame in a rig test."
